---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy" description="How this website collects, uses and protects information, including messages sent through the contact form.">
  <div class="container">
    <article class="legal">
      <p>
        This policy explains what information this website collects, how it is used, and the choices you have. By using the site or sending a message through the contact form, you agree to the practices described here.
      </p>
      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p>
        When you use the contact form we collect the details you enter: your name, email address, phone number, date of birth, your message, and any image you attach. We use your date of birth only to confirm that you are old enough to be tattooed.
      </p>
      <p>
        Like most websites, our hosting provider may automatically record technical information such as your IP address, browser type and the pages you visit. This information is used to keep the site running securely and is not used to identify you personally.
      </p>
      <h2>How we use your information</h2>
      <p>
        We use the details you send to reply to your enquiry, to discuss and schedule appointments, and to prepare for your session. We do not sell your information, and we do not use it for advertising.
      </p>
      <h2>Who receives your information</h2>
      <p>
        Messages from the contact form are delivered to the studio by email through an email delivery service. The site is hosted on Cloudflare. The contact form is protected by Google reCAPTCHA, which checks that a person is sending the message; Google's privacy policy and terms of service apply to that check. The site also embeds a Google Map on the contact page, which means Google may receive your IP address when it loads. We do not share your information with anyone else unless the law requires it.
      </p>
      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site does not set its own cookies and does not use analytics or advertising trackers. Third-party services such as Google reCAPTCHA and Google Maps may set their own cookies when they load.
      </p>
      <h2>How long we keep information</h2>
      <p>
        We keep enquiries and any related correspondence for as long as needed to respond to you and to keep a record of work carried out, and then delete them. You can ask us to delete your information at any time.
      </p>
      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask to see, correct or delete the personal information we hold about you by contacting us using the details on the contact page. If you would rather not use the form, you can email us directly.
      </p>
      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is not intended for anyone under 18, and we do not knowingly collect information from children.
      </p>
      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. The current version is always the one on this page.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be sent using the details on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
